<title>JAPAN: Shinagawa Refractories falls sharply on report.</title>
<headline>Shinagawa Refractories falls sharply on report.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Shinagawa Refractories Co Ltd, a major manufacturer of refractory materials for steelmakers, fell sharply on Monday.</p>
<p>Sales were triggered by a major research institute's report that it would keep a cautious stance on the share price, traders said.</p>
<p>At 0525 GMT, the share was down 95 yen at 865 yen, making it the third-steepest percentage loser on the first section of the Tokyo Stock Exchange.</p>
